          <toggle-section open="false">
            <h3>Video transcript </h3>
            <p><strong>Jack:</strong> Let's look at different technologies that use code to run.</p>
<p>The Internet of Things or IoT are becoming commonplace in our lives today and the range of items that use coding to run are expanding all the time. IoT technologies that use code to work, include coffee machines, light bulbs, showers, cooking appliances and baby monitoring equipment to name but a few. Coding can help programme our appliances to know where we are, what time we get up, how healthy we are, what we like to eat and even how we like it cooked.</p>
<p><strong>Leah:</strong> Smart heating and lighting in our smart homes can help to keep us cool or warm us up, making sure our homes are ready for us when we return’ with the lights turned on for us and even in a range of colours of our choosing.</p>
<p>Wearable tech can monitor our fitness and health telling us when to move and when to sit down, helping us to reach our fitness goals and making sure we stay healthy in the process and sleep well at night.</p>
<p><strong>Jack:</strong> When we shower after a run or when we wake up in the morning the temperature of the shower and time we shower for, can be monitored for economic purposes.</p>
<p>Tech savvy parents can monitor their babies to alleviate their anxieties using monitoring equipment, smart clothing, temperature control and monitoring and watch over them with smart toys.</p>
<p><strong>Leah:</strong> We use coded programmed systems to help us purchase goods and have them delivered or pick them up. We use it to help us travel nationally on public transport and for international travel. Electric cars can tell us where to go, how to get there and can even take the controls themselves and drive us there at times.</p>
<p><strong>Jack:</strong> We have now moved from coding and programming being involved in just computer-based systems which carry the data on us and our lives. Mobile digital devices and smart phones and IoT gives us the opportunity through coding and programming to be always connected to all things social, work and play.</p>
<p><strong>Leah:</strong> It's amazing to think of all the common objects and things we use today that are programmed to run code, and how it affects our life and the way we live it. It also means that there is a vast world of coding and programming needs out there, and jobs for those who want to get involved in the industry and see in the next wave of advancements and additions.</p>

          </toggle-section>
        
      
          
